<h2>9. Spectroscopy & Chromatography Suite (8 Analytical Techniques)</h2>
<p>
  The Spectroscopy Hub covers the 8 core analytical and spectroscopic methods central to postgraduate chemical analysis.
</p>

<h3>The 8 Analytical Techniques</h3>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Reverse-Phase HPLC (Chromatography):</strong> Retention factor ($k'$), resolution ($R_s$), theoretical plate count ($N$), and peak asymmetry/tailing ($T_f$).</li>
  <li><strong>Gas Chromatography (Chromatography):</strong> Kovats retention index ($I$), Van Deemter equation ($H = A + B/u + Cu$), and carrier gas optimization.</li>
  <li><strong>Thin Layer Chromatography (Chromatography):</strong> Retention factor ($R_f = d_{	ext{solute}} / d_{	ext{solvent}}$) and mobile phase polarity screening.</li>
  <li><strong>500 MHz 1H NMR (Spectroscopy):</strong> Chemical shift values ($\delta$, ppm), scalar coupling constants ($J$, Hz), proton integration, and multiplicity splitting patterns.</li>
  <li><strong>13C DEPT NMR (Spectroscopy):</strong> Carbon-13 chemical shifts with DEPT-45, DEPT-90, and DEPT-135 discrimination of quaternary, CH, CH2, and CH3 carbons.</li>
  <li><strong>FT-IR Spectroscopy (Spectroscopy):</strong> Characteristic functional group stretching frequencies ($ar{
u}$, $	ext{cm}^{-1}$), Hooke's law calculations, and reduced mass ($\mu$).</li>
  <li><strong>Mass Spectrometry (Spectroscopy):</strong> Molecular ion ($M^+$), base peak, isotope abundance clusters ($M+1$, $M+2$ for Cl and Br), and fragmentation pathways (McLafferty rearrangement, alpha-cleavage).</li>
  <li><strong>UV-Visible Spectroscopy (Spectroscopy):</strong> Beer-Lambert law ($A = arepsilon c l$), $\lambda_{\max}$ estimation via Woodward-Fieser rules for conjugated dienes and enones.</li>
</ol>

<h3>Interactive Spectrogram Navigation</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>2D Pan & Pinch Zoom (1.0x to 5.0x):</strong> Smooth multi-touch inspection of fine splitting patterns and multiplet peaks.</li>
  <li><strong>Dedicated Zoom Toolbar:</strong> On-screen controls for Zoom In (+), Zoom Out (-), and View Reset (1.0x).</li>
  <li><strong>Haptic Peak Snapping:</strong> Tapping near any spectral peak engages haptic feedback and displays a precise crosshair with exact chemical shift ($\delta$), retention time ($t_R$), or wavenumber ($	ext{cm}^{-1}$).</li>
  <li><strong>Mathematical Formulations:</strong> All governing equations and physical definitions are rendered in standard mathematical typography.</li>
</ul>

