<h2>12. Pericyclic Hub & Woodward-Hoffmann FMO Symmetry Engine</h2>
<p>
  Pericyclic reactions are governed by orbital symmetry conservation principles. ChemBuddy incorporates a Frontier Molecular Orbital (FMO) selection engine:
</p>

<h3>Woodward-Hoffmann Selection Rules Matrix</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Reaction Type</th>
      <th>Electron System</th>
      <th>Thermal ($\Delta$) Mode</th>
      <th>Photochemical ($h
u$) Mode</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td rowspan="2"><strong>Electrocyclic Reactions</strong></td>
      <td>$4n$ electrons (e.g., 1,3-Butadiene)</td>
      <td><strong>Conrotatory</strong> (HOMO $\psi_2$, $C_2$ symmetry)</td>
      <td><strong>Disrotatory</strong> (HOMO $\psi_3$, $m$ symmetry)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>$4n+2$ electrons (e.g., 1,3,5-Hexatriene)</td>
      <td><strong>Disrotatory</strong> (HOMO $\psi_3$, $m$ symmetry)</td>
      <td><strong>Conrotatory</strong> (HOMO $\psi_4$, $C_2$ symmetry)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td rowspan="2"><strong>Cycloadditions</strong></td>
      <td>$4n$ electrons (e.g., $[2+2]$)</td>
      <td>Symmetry Forbidden ($[\pi 2s + \pi 2s]$)</td>
      <td><strong>Symmetry Allowed</strong> ($[\pi 2s + \pi 2s]$)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>$4n+2$ electrons (e.g., $[4+2]$ Diels-Alder)</td>
      <td><strong>Symmetry Allowed</strong> ($[\pi 4s + \pi 2s]$, Endo preference)</td>
      <td>Symmetry Forbidden ($[\pi 4s + \pi 2s]$)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td rowspan="2"><strong>Sigmatropic Rearrangements</strong></td>
      <td>$[1,3]$ Hydrogen Shift</td>
      <td>Symmetry Forbidden (Suprafacial)</td>
      <td><strong>Symmetry Allowed</strong> (Suprafacial)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>$[1,5]$ & $[3,3]$ (Cope, Claisen)</td>
      <td><strong>Symmetry Allowed</strong> (Suprafacial, Chair-like transition state)</td>
      <td>Symmetry Forbidden</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- CHAPTER 13 -->
