<h2>13. Smart Timetable & Attendance Intelligence Engine</h2>
<p>
  The attendance module in ChemBuddy is an analytical forecasting engine designed to ensure strict compliance with university regulations.
</p>

<h3>The 75% Cutoff Mathematics</h3>
<p>
  Most universities enforce a mandatory <strong>75% attendance threshold</strong> for semester examination eligibility. ChemBuddy computes two critical metrics:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Classes Needed to Recover 75% (Target Equation):</strong>
    <p>If current attendance is below 75%, ChemBuddy solves:</p>
    <div class="formula-box">$$	ext{Classes Needed} = \max\left(0, \lceil 3 	imes 	ext{Absent} - 	ext{Present} ceilight)$$</div>
    <p>This reveals the exact number of consecutive classes a student must attend without missing a single lecture to restore eligibility.</p>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Safe Classes That Can Be Skipped (Buffer Equation):</strong>
    <p>If current attendance is safely above 75%, ChemBuddy solves:</p>
    <div class="formula-box">$$	ext{Safe Bunks Available} = \max\left(0, \lfloor (	ext{Present} - 3 	imes 	ext{Absent}) / 3 flooright)$$</div>
    <p>This informs the student how many lectures they can afford to miss for conferences, medical reasons, or emergencies while remaining strictly at or above 75.0%.</p>
  </li>
</ol>

<h3>Supported Attendance Statuses</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Status</th>
      <th>Effect on Percentage</th>
      <th>Academic Use Case</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Present (✅)</strong></td>
      <td>Increments both Present and Total Count</td>
      <td>Student attended lecture or practical session.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Absent (❌)</strong></td>
      <td>Increments Total Count; Present count unchanged</td>
      <td>Student missed lecture or was marked absent.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Postponed / Cancelled (⏸️)</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Excluded entirely from calculation</strong></td>
      <td>Faculty was absent, institutional holiday, or lab rescheduled. Does not penalize the student's attendance.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Excused / On Duty (OD)</strong></td>
      <td>Treated as Present</td>
      <td>Official university duty, symposium, seminar presentation, or authorized medical leave.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

