<h2>15. Exporting Attendance Records (Institutional PDF & Excel XLV/CSV)</h2>
<p>
  To facilitate submission to university faculties, academic advisors, and department heads, ChemBuddy provides multi-format attendance report generation.
</p>

<h3>Institutional Attendance Reports</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Institutional PDF Report:</strong> Formatted with official university headers, student registration number, department name, subject-wise lecture breakdown (Total, Attended, Missed, Percentage), and eligibility status certification.</li>
  <li><strong>Excel Spreadsheet (XLV/CSV):</strong> Formatted with a UTF-8 Byte Order Mark (BOM) for compatibility with Microsoft Excel, featuring date-stamped audit logs of every attendance event.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 16 -->
<h2>16. Smart Flashcards & Spaced Repetition (SuperMemo-2 Active Recall)</h2>
<p>
  ChemBuddy implements the <strong>SuperMemo-2 (SM-2) algorithm</strong> to support long-term memorization of reaction mechanisms, reagents, and spectroscopic data.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Active Recall Testing:</strong> Cards present a prompt or starting material first. Students formulate the product or mechanism mentally before flipping the card.</li>
  <li><strong>Recall Quality Rating (1 to 4):</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><code>Again (1)</code>: Complete failure of recall; card repeats in current session.</li>
      <li><code>Hard (2)</code>: Recalled with significant difficulty; review interval expands slowly.</li>
      <li><code>Good (3)</code>: Correct recall with normal effort; optimal interval expansion.</li>
      <li><code>Easy (4)</code>: Instant, confident recall; interval expands significantly.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Automated Deck Generation:</strong> Converts uploaded notes and mechanism summaries into interactive flashcard sets.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 17 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>17. PDF Library, Study Hub & Grounded Academic RAG Assistant</h2>
<p>
  The PDF Library allows students to store, organize, and search their textbooks, syllabus documents, and research papers.
</p>

<h3>Single-Source Grounding Architecture</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Strictly Grounded Retrieval:</strong> In the PDF Study Hub, the AI assistant is constrained strictly to the extracted text of the uploaded PDF document.</li>
  <li><strong>Standardized Refusal:</strong> If a query is outside the scope of the provided document, the assistant explicitly states: <em>"This topic is not covered in the provided document."</em> to avoid hallucinated information.</li>
  <li><strong>Extended Token Output:</strong> Supports comprehensive, detailed answers (up to 8,192 tokens) complete with KaTeX mathematical formatting and structural ASCII diagrams.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 18 -->
<h2>18. Exam Mode & BCU Model Answer Generator</h2>
<p>
  Calibrated to Bangalore City University (BCU) and Indian university examination patterns:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>2-Mark Question Mode:</strong> Concise, precise definitions, IUPAC names, and fundamental statements.</li>
  <li><strong>5-Mark Question Mode:</strong> Step-by-step mechanisms, curved arrow notations, and intermediate structures.</li>
  <li><strong>10-Mark Question Mode:</strong> Comprehensive essays, retro-synthetic analysis, multi-step synthesis routes, and spectroscopic confirmation.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 19 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>19. Daily Cognitive & Learning Science Facts (120+ Curated Insights)</h2>
<p>
  Postgraduate study requires sustained mental focus and emotional resilience. ChemBuddy includes a curated library of 120+ evidence-based cognitive psychology insights:
</p>

<div class="feature-grid">
  <div class="feature-box">
    <h4>1. Cognitive Biases & Heuristics</h4>
    <p>Zeigarnik Effect, Halo Effect, Dunning-Kruger Effect, Spotlight Effect, Framing Effect, Anchoring Bias, Loss Aversion, Sunk Cost Fallacy, and Dual-Process Theory.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-box">
    <h4>2. Memory & Learning Psychology</h4>
    <p>Ebbinghaus Forgetting Curve, Testing Effect, Serial Position Effect (Primacy & Recency), State-Dependent Memory, Sleep Consolidation, and Generation Effect.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-box">
    <h4>3. Neurobiology & Focus</h4>
    <p>Dopamine Anticipation, Neuroplasticity, Ultradian Rhythms (90-min cycles), Amygdala Regulation, and Sleep Spindles.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-box">
    <h4>4. Habits & Academic Performance</h4>
    <p>The 20-Second Rule, Implementation Intentions ("If-Then"), Parkinson's Law, Decision Fatigue, and Daily 1% Compounding.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>Prime-Weighted Non-Repeating Distribution Formula</h3>
<p>
  To guarantee that every day presents a distinct, non-repeating insight across the academic calendar, ChemBuddy employs a deterministic distribution formula:
</p>
<div class="formula-box">$$	ext{Index} = \left( 	ext{Year} 	imes 365 + 	ext{DayOfYear} 	imes 47 + 	ext{Month} 	imes 13 ight) \pmod{	ext{TotalFacts}}$$</div>

<!-- CHAPTER 20 -->
<h2>20. Laboratory Safety & GHS Hazard Library</h2>
<p>
  Essential for laboratory research scholars and postgraduate practical examinations:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>GHS Pictograms & Hazard Codes:</strong> Explanations of H-statements (Hazard Statements) and P-statements (Precautionary Statements).</li>
  <li><strong>Chemical Incompatibility Matrix:</strong> Identifies hazardous reagent combinations (e.g., strong oxidizers with organic solvents, water-reactive organometallics).</li>
  <li><strong>First Aid Protocols:</strong> Immediate emergency response steps for acid burns, alkali exposure, inhalation of toxic vapors, and solvent spills.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 21 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>21. Offline Security, Local Encrypted Storage & Data Portability</h2>
<p>
  ChemBuddy operates with a strict local-first data architecture:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Encrypted Local Storage:</strong> Student profiles, attendance logs, notes, and preferences are stored in encrypted binary format on the user's device.</li>
  <li><strong>Complete Data Portability:</strong> Students can export their entire profile, timetable, and attendance records as a structured JSON file at any time for backup.</li>
  <li><strong>Zero Unsolicited Data Transmission:</strong> The application does not transmit student personal data, attendance logs, or sketcher data to external servers.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 22 -->
<h2>22. Troubleshooting & Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>

<div class="callout callout-warning">
  <div class="callout-title">Q1: Why did the 8:30 AM morning timetable notification not trigger?</div>
  <p><strong>Resolution:</strong> On Android 12+, confirm that <em>"Alarms & Reminders"</em> permission is granted in Android System Settings. Additionally, set battery optimization for ChemBuddy to <em>"Unrestricted"</em> so that the system's background Doze mode does not defer morning alarms.</p>
</div>

<div class="callout callout-warning">
  <div class="callout-title">Q2: Can coordination complexes and organometallics be sketched in ChemDraw Pro?</div>
  <p><strong>Resolution:</strong> Yes. Open the 118-element periodic table palette, select the transition metal center (e.g., Fe, Co, Ni, Pt), and use coordination bonds. Pre-configured templates for <em>Ferrocene</em> and <em>Porphyrin</em> are also available.</p>
</div>

<div class="callout callout-warning">
  <div class="callout-title">Q3: How does ChemBuddy handle attendance for cancelled or rescheduled lectures?</div>
  <p><strong>Resolution:</strong> Mark the lecture as <em>Postponed / Cancelled (⏸️)</em>. ChemBuddy removes that class slot from both the numerator and denominator, ensuring the student's percentage is not unfairly penalized.</p>
</div>

<div class="callout callout-warning">
  <div class="callout-title">Q4: Does reaction prediction or SVG generation require an active internet connection?</div>
  <p><strong>Resolution:</strong> No. The offline reaction rule engine and the <code>SmilesSvgGenerator</code> vector layout engine run entirely on-device with zero latency.</p>
</div>

<div class="callout callout-warning">
  <div class="callout-title">Q5: How can attendance records and reaction mechanisms be presented to university faculty?</div>
  <p><strong>Resolution:</strong> Use the built-in export engine to generate either an official Academic PDF Dossier (formatted with margins, headers, and mechanisms) or an Excel Spreadsheet (XLV/CSV) with UTF-8 BOM encoding for direct opening in Microsoft Excel.</p>
</div>

